@* Shown on the sign-in page when no Google OAuth client is configured, with
   the exact commands to set one -- the same pattern as MapConfigNotice. *@

<div class="card-panel auth-fallback">
    <p class="auth-fallback-title">Sign-in isn't configured yet.</p>
    <p>
        Create an OAuth client ID (type "Web application") in Google Cloud
        Console, add <code>/signin-google</code> on this site's origin as an
        authorised redirect URI, then from the <code>MelanomaDetection.Web</code>
        project folder run:
    </p>
    <p><code class="auth-fallback-command">dotnet user-secrets set "Authentication:Google:ClientId" "your-client-id"</code></p>
    <p><code class="auth-fallback-command">dotnet user-secrets set "Authentication:Google:ClientSecret" "your-client-secret"</code></p>
    <p class="auth-fallback-last">then restart the app. See README.md for the Docker equivalent.</p>
</div>
